{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Yang2011-34-layer-PBS-632nm",
  "Source": "K. Yang, X. Long, Y. Huang, and S. Wu, \"Design and fabrication of ultra-high precision thin-film polarizing beam splitter,\" Opt. Commun. 284, 4650-4653 (2011). doi:10.1016/j.optcom.2011.06.038 - Text p. 4651, coating structure string S/71.9H/111.8L/.../68.5L/A; target in Table 1",
  "Notes": "Thin-film polarizing beam splitter: transmit P, reflect S at 64.8 deg angle of incidence around 632.8 nm\nSpecification: Table 1: at 64.8 deg angle of incidence, over 632.8 +/- 10 nm, Ts < 0.02 % and Tp > 99.98 %.\nReported: At 632.8 nm, 64.8 deg: Rs = 0.999966, Rp = 1 ppm (theoretical). Fig. 1: Ts < ~0.05 % from 602.8 to ~650 nm rising to ~3.5 % at 662.8 nm; Tp > ~99 % from ~617.8 to ~650 nm, ~30 % at 602.8 nm and ~92 % at 662.8 nm. Fig. 3: theoretical Ts ~2e-5 at 628 nm rising to ~8e-5 at 637.8 nm. Fig. 4(a): at normal incidence, high-reflectance band ~600-750 nm with transmittance peaks near 515, 540, 565, 575 nm. Measured Rp at 632.8 nm vs angle (Table 2): 62.5 deg 0.237 %, 63.0 0.165 %, 63.5 0.105 %, 64.0 0.058 %, 64.5 0.026 %, 65.0 0.010 %, 65.5 0.009 %, 66.0 0.026 %, 66.5 0.061 %, 67.0 0.118 %; interpolated 0.017 % at 64.8 deg. Theoretical Rp minimum is near 65 deg (Fig. 4b).\nNotes: The paper writes the stack from the substrate outward (S/71.9H/111.8L/.../75.5H/68.5L/A); it has been reversed here so layer 1 (68.5 nm L) touches the incident medium and layer 34 (71.9 nm H) touches the substrate. 34 layers, total ~3188 nm, consistent with Fig. 2(a). 'A' is called 'outer space' (air); the 64.8 deg angle is taken as the angle in air (Rp vs incident angle is measured in air, Fig. 4b). The introduction defines theta0 for MacNeille cubes as the angle in the substrate, but that condition cannot be met here and the device is a plate on fused silica, so air incidence is assumed. Substrate index 1.457 (fused silica) given as a constant; materials are 'considered to be perfect dielectrics' (k = 0). The H/L materials are not named. Back surface of the substrate is not discussed (single-surface coating calculation assumed). Layer 6 counted from the substrate is 115.44 nm (two decimals, as printed). Merit step size not given.\nLayers from Text p. 4651, coating structure string S/71.9H/111.8L/.../68.5L/A; target in Table 1; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours Rs 0.999967, Rp 1.95 ppm at 632.8 nm, 64.8 deg; paper Rs 0.999966, Rp 1 ppm.",
